---
import PillBadge from '../ui/PillBadge.astro';
import PullQuote from '../ui/PullQuote.astro';
import ResponsiveImage from '../ui/ResponsiveImage.astro';
import ScrollReveal from '../ui/ScrollReveal.astro';
---

<section class="section-y bg-bone">
  <div class="container-edge">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[760px]">
      <ScrollReveal stagger class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <div class="reveal">
          <PillBadge>A short history of the strategic move</PillBadge>
        </div>

        <h2
          class="reveal font-display text-ink text-balance"
          style="font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.06; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 380;"
        >
          Every successful immigrant economy in the last hundred years started with the same kind of person.
        </h2>

        <p class="reveal text-[1.15rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted md:text-[1.2rem]">
          Not the desperate. The strategic.
        </p>
      </ScrollReveal>

      <ScrollReveal class="mt-12">
        <figure
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border-soft bg-bone-deeper shadow-card"
          data-history-figure
        >
          <ResponsiveImage
            base="/images/history-ny-1933"
            widths={[800, 1200, 1600]}
            sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 760px, 100vw"
            alt="Three men in overcoats and fedoras outside the Western Trust Company on a New York street, 1933."
            ratio="3/2"
            imgClass="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-[1400ms] ease-editorial will-change-transform"
          />
          <figcaption class="border-t border-border-soft bg-bone-soft px-5 py-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-soft">
            New York, 1933 &middot; The strategic move, before the storm.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </ScrollReveal>

      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-7">
        <ScrollReveal>
          <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink md:text-[1.1rem]">
            The European entrepreneurs who left between the wars didn't know exactly what was coming. They knew enough. The ones who moved early rebuilt fortunes in New York, London, S&atilde;o Paulo. The ones who waited too long lost everything.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
        <div class="hairline"></div>

        <ScrollReveal>
          <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink md:text-[1.1rem]">
            The Cubans who left Havana in 1959 didn't know Castro would last. They knew enough. Their grandchildren run South Florida. The families that stayed lost everything to nationalization within four years.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
        <div class="hairline"></div>

        <ScrollReveal>
          <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink md:text-[1.1rem]">
            The Hong Kongers who left in 2019 didn't know the National Security Law was coming in 2020. They knew enough. They're now in London, Vancouver, Singapore. The ones who waited are now subject to a different legal system than they were born into.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
        <div class="hairline"></div>

        <ScrollReveal>
          <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink md:text-[1.1rem]">
            Every wave shares two patterns. The ones who moved did so because they could <strong class="font-medium text-ink">read the math</strong>, not because they had to. And once they were settled, they outperformed the natives in their adopted countries within a generation.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal>
          <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted md:text-[1.1rem]">
            The strategy is two centuries old:
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 mb-14 flex justify-center">
        <ScrollReveal>
          <PullQuote>
            The cost of moving early is paperwork. The cost of moving late is everything.
          </PullQuote>
        </ScrollReveal>
      </div>

      <ScrollReveal class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-left">
        <p class="text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-ink md:text-[1.1rem]">
          The mechanism &mdash; moving cleanly, in 90 days, without losing your business in the process &mdash; is what hasn't existed.
        </p>
        <p
          class="font-display italic text-oxblood"
          style="font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.7rem); line-height: 1.25; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 360;"
        >
          Until now.
        </p>
      </ScrollReveal>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
